It's differentiable, right?

01:12:35.600 --> 01:12:36.230
So nice.

01:12:36.230 --> 01:12:36.950
I can do that.

01:12:36.950 --> 01:12:39.110
And now, I suddenly get a
learned compressor, which

01:12:39.110 --> 01:12:40.910
is more optimized for SSIM.

01:12:40.910 --> 01:12:43.250
And it will probably
already perform better

01:12:43.250 --> 01:12:49.350
